  level was dropped so the tutorial can refer to `deploy/g1_29dof/`).
* 22 files in total are byte-identical to upstream.

What we changed (Apache-2.0 §4(b): these files carry our modifications)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. `deploy/g1_29dof/CMakeLists.txt`
   a) ONNX Runtime location is now taken from the `ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT` environment
      variable when it is set, and only falls back to the bundled
      `thirdparty/onnxruntime-linux-x64-1.22.0` path when it is not. Reason: our
      students install ONNX Runtime through `deploy/install_onnxruntime.sh`, which
      may place it in their home directory.
   b) Added two configure-time existence checks (header + shared library) that
      abort with the exact commands to run. Upstream configures happily even when
      the directory is missing, and the failure only shows up later as
      `fatal error: onnxruntime_cxx_api.h: No such file or directory` during
      `make` — which students cannot connect back to the cause.

2. `deploy/g1_29dof/config/config.yaml`
   The two Mimic FSM entries (`Mimic_Dance_102`, `Mimic_Gangnam_Style`) and
   their joystick transitions are commented out by default, with an inline
   note explaining how to re-enable them. Reason: they require a Mimic policy
   and a motion-capture CSV that this teaching repository does not ship; an
   out-of-the-box student build otherwise selects a state with no model behind
   it.

